## To test dockerignore you can use - `rsync -avn . /dev/shm --exclude-from .dockerignore`
## shows a list of all the files that will be included in the image
## Ref - https://stackoverflow.com/questions/38946683/how-to-test-dockerignore-file


# exclude bin and .git folders
**/bin
**/.git

# ignore .gitlab-ci.yaml 
.gitlab-ci.yml

# ignore unwanted deploy dirs
deploy/docker-compose
deploy/kustomize

# ignore markdown files
*.md

# ...except the third-party notices, which must ship with the image: the image
# is the distributed artifact, and Apache-2.0 4(d) and the MIT/BSD "include
# this notice in all copies" clauses attach to the thing distributed, not to
# this repo. Negation must stay after the *.md rule above to take effect.
!THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
